### Missing rate -> 400: "Please enter the rate"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/simple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "find": "AMOUNT",
  "principal": 8000,
  "time": 2,
  "unit": 1
}

### Several things missing at once -> 400 with a list of messages
POST http://localhost:8080/api/simple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "find": "RATE"
}

### Rate of zero -> 400: "Rate must be greater than 0"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/simple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "find": "AMOUNT",
  "principal": 8000,
  "rate": 0,
  "time": 2,
  "unit": 1
}

### Negative principal -> 400: "Principal must be greater than 0"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/simple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "find": "AMOUNT",
  "principal": -500,
  "rate": 7,
  "time": 2,
  "unit": 1
}

### A "find" value that does not exist -> 400: "The request could not be read..."
POST http://localhost:8080/api/simple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "find": "BANANA",
  "principal": 8000,
  "rate": 7,
  "time": 2,
  "unit": 1
}

### Time unit outside 1 to 6 -> 400: "Time unit must be a number from 1 to 6"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/simple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "find": "AMOUNT",
  "principal": 8000,
  "rate": 7,
  "time": 2,
  "unit": 9
}

### Amount smaller than principal when finding the rate -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/simple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "find": "RATE",
  "known": "AMOUNT",
  "principal": 8000,
  "amount": 7000,
  "time": 2,
  "unit": 1
}

### Compound: timesPerYear not allowed -> 400: "timesPerYear must be 1, 2, 4, 12, 52 or 360"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/compound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "find": "AMOUNT",
  "principal": 10000,
  "rate": 10,
  "time": 2,
  "unit": 1,
  "timesPerYear": 5
}

### Compound: numbers so big the result can't be shown -> 400: "too big or cannot be calculated"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/compound
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "find": "AMOUNT",
  "principal": 10000,
  "rate": 1000,
  "time": 100000,
  "unit": 1,
  "timesPerYear": 360
}
